            <title>[LU-21230] sanity-lnet test_291, test_292 fail when conns_per_peer &gt; 1</title>
                <link>https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-21230</link>
                <project id="10000" key="LU">Lustre</project>
                    <description>&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Problem"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Problem&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;sanity-lnet test_291 and test_292 fail on a node whose NIC reports a link speed of 4 Gb/s or more. Both tests expect socklnd to use conns_per_peer=1. socklnd sets conns_per_peer from the link speed, so the tests fail on fast links.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;div class="preformatted panel" style="border-width: 1px;"&gt;&lt;div class="preformattedContent panelContent"&gt;
&lt;pre&gt;sanity-lnet test_291: @@@@@@ FAIL: failed to set conns-per-peer to 1
sanity-lnet test_292: @@@@@@ FAIL: expected 2 tcp connections on port 7988
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Environment"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Environment&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;master at 7c3c9f8814 (&lt;a href="https://jira.whamcloud.com/browse/LU-20076" title="reduce testing time by optimizing test and test-framework.sh" class="issue-link" data-issue-key="LU-20076"&gt;LU-20076&lt;/a&gt;)&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;rocky9 aarch64 VM, tcp NETTYPE, virtio-net NIC that reports 100000 Mb/s&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Reproduction"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Reproduction&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Use a node with a NIC that reports 100 Gb/s in &lt;tt&gt;ethtool&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
	&lt;li&gt;Run &lt;tt&gt;ONLY="291 292" bash sanity-lnet.sh&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;


&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Analysis"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Analysis&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ksocklnd_speed2cpp() returns ilog2(speed / 1000) / 2 + 1. A 100 Gb/s link gives conns_per_peer=4. A NIC with no speed gives 1. We think that the CI VMs report no link speed. That would explain why CI does not see the failure.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Test 291 checks for &lt;tt&gt;conns_per_peer: 1&lt;/tt&gt; and fails at once. Test 292 expects 1 control connection and 1 bulk connection on the acceptor port. But socklnd makes conns_per_peer bulk connections. At 100 Gb/s, test 292 sees 5 connections and times out.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;h2&gt;&lt;a name="Proposedfix"&gt;&lt;/a&gt;Proposed fix&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Read conns_per_peer from &lt;tt&gt;lnetctl net show -v&lt;/tt&gt;. Expect conns_per_peer bulk connections in test_291, and 1 + conns_per_peer connections in test_292.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
